Below is a self-contained Python function that attempts to rename and/or reorder the column headers of an xudf table object df0 using either a mapping (dict0) or an ordering sequence (lst0). Because different table-like objects expose different APIs (pandas-like, xudf-specific, or SQL-like select/alias), the function tries several common approaches in a safe order and raises a clear error if none succeed. It returns a new table when it cannot perform the operation in-place; if an in-place change is performed it returns the same object (or None if the underlying API mutates in-place and returns None).

Usage summary:
- Provide dict0 to rename columns (mapping old_name -> new_name).
- Provide lst0 to reorder columns (list of column names in desired order). lst0 may refer to the original names or to the names after dict0 renaming; if both dict0 and lst0 are provided the renaming is applied first then the reorder.
- Set inplace=True to prefer mutating df0 when the underlying API supports it.

